#Direct Boolean Returning -> Writing something like the num1 > num2 evalutes the maths and sends the raw True and False back instantly. You don't need some big block of if-else statement to do that.
#The Early Return Pattern -> Think of it like you want to return something, you could have used print() or if-else statement but there is a better solution for that. Return statement exits the loop and let the result in the return be accessable by the external functions and print() only gives the output to the console but who will exit the function and make the result accessable to the others and if-else statement is where you can simple use return to avoid the complexcity of printing various messages.
